《張釋之馮唐列傳》
張釋之 was a native of 堵陽, named 張釋之, with the courtesy name 季. He had an elder brother 仲 who lived with him. He was made a 騎郎 by means of his fortune, serving 孝文帝. For ten years he was not promoted, and he was not known for anything. 張釋之 said, "My long service has reduced my brother's estate, and it has not gone well." He wanted to resign and return home. 中郎將 袁盎 knew his worth, grieved at his departure, and so requested that 張釋之 be transferred to 謁者. After 張釋之 had finished his morning audience, he approached and spoke of matters beneficial to the state. 文帝 said, "Be modest, do not speak too high-flown, but say what can be implemented now." Then 張釋之 spoke of the affairs of the 秦 and 漢, and for a long time why 秦 had lost and 漢 had risen. 文帝 praised him as good, and then appointed 張釋之 as 謁者仆射.
張釋之 accompanied the emperor on a journey and ascended the 虎圈. The emperor asked the 上林尉 about the roster of the beasts, asking more than ten questions. The 尉 and his attendants looked around, all unable to answer. The 虎圈嗇夫 from the side answered the emperor's questions about the roster of beasts very thoroughly, wanting to observe his ability to answer orally and respond without end. 文帝 said, "The official should not be like this? The 尉 is worthless!" Then he ordered 張釋之 to appoint the 嗇夫 as 上林令. 張釋之 went forward after a while and said, "Your Majesty, how is 絳侯 周勃?" The emperor said, "He is a 長者." He asked again, "How is 東陽侯 張相?" The emperor again said, "He is a 長者." 張釋之 said, "The 絳侯 and 東陽侯 are called 長者, but these two men, when speaking of affairs, could not even get words out, how could they match this 嗇夫's clever, glib, and quick tongue? Moreover, 秦 relied on 刀筆之吏, and the officials competed to surpass each other by being quick and harsh in investigation, but their only effect was empty formalities, without the real compassion. Therefore, their faults were not heard, and they declined until the 二世, and the world collapsed. Now Your Majesty, because of the 嗇夫's eloquence, has promoted him beyond measure, I fear that the world will follow the wind, all competing to be glib-tongued without substance. Moreover, the lower orders are influenced by the upper orders faster than the shadow by the light, so actions must not be taken lightly." 文帝 said, "Good." Then he stopped appointing the 嗇夫.
The emperor was about to mount his carriage, and summoned 張釋之 to ride as 參乘, slowly rode, and asked 張釋之 about the decline of 秦. He answered fully and frankly. Upon reaching the palace, the emperor appointed 張釋之 as 公車令.
After a while, the 太子 and 梁王 rode together into the palace, not alighting at the 司馬門. Then 張釋之 pursued and stopped the 太子 and 梁王 from entering the 殿門. He then accused them of not alighting at the 公門, disrespectfully, and reported it. 薄太后 heard of it, and 文帝 removed his cap and apologized, saying, "I taught my son badly." 薄太后 then sent an envoy to receive the emperor's order to pardon the 太子 and 梁王, and only then were they allowed in. 文帝 thereafter regarded 張釋之 as extraordinary, and appointed him as 中大夫.
After a while, he became 中郎將. Accompanying the emperor on a journey to 霸陵, he stayed at the northern 臨廁. At that time 慎夫人 was with him, and the emperor pointed to 慎夫人 the 新豐道, saying, "This is the road to 邯鄲." He had 慎夫人 play the 瑟, and the emperor himself leaned on the 瑟 and sang, with a sorrowful and mournful heart, and turned to the 群臣 and said, "Alas! If we use 北山石 as a coffin, use 紵絮 to cut and line it, and smear 漆 in the gaps, how could it be moved?" The attendants all said, "Good." 張釋之 advanced and said, "If there is something desirable inside, even if it is enclosed in 南山, there is still a gap; if there is nothing desirable inside, even without a stone coffin, what sorrow is there?" 文帝 praised him as good. Afterward, he appointed 張釋之 as 廷尉.
After a while, the emperor went out from 中渭橋, and a man ran out from under the bridge, startling the emperor's horse. Then he sent a 騎 to capture him, and referred him to the 廷尉. 張釋之 investigated. He said, "The county man came, heard the 蹕, hid under the bridge. After a while, thinking the procession had passed, he came out, saw the emperor's carriage and cavalry, and ran." The 廷尉 秦當 was correct: one person violating the 蹕 should be fined. 文帝 was angry and said, "This man personally startled my horse, my horse relied on softness and harmony, if I used another horse, it would certainly not be injured? Yet the 廷尉 only fined him!" 張釋之 said, "The law is what the emperor and the world share. If the law is like this and is made heavier, then the law is not believed by the people. Moreover, at that time, if the emperor had ordered him to be executed, it would have been done. Now that he has been referred to the 廷尉, the 廷尉 is the balance of the world, if it tips, then all the world's laws become light or heavy, and the people do not know where to put their hands and feet. Please, Your Majesty, examine this." After a long time, the emperor said, "The 廷尉 was right."
Afterward, a man stole a 玉環 from the 高廟, was captured, and 文帝 was angry, referring him to the 廷尉 for investigation. 張釋之 examined the law: stealing the 宗廟's 服御物 was to be reported, and the report should be that he should be executed by 棄市. The emperor was very angry and said, "The people's lack of virtue, to steal the relics of the former emperor's shrine, I have entrusted the 廷尉 to cause him to be 族, but you, by law, report him, this is not what I intend to share in the 宗廟." 張釋之 removed his cap, bowed his head, and apologized, saying, "The law is sufficient. Moreover, the crimes are equal, but they differ in 逆順. Now to cause him to be 族 for stealing the 宗廟's relics, if there is a one in ten thousand chance, suppose a foolish commoner takes a handful of earth from 長陵, what would Your Majesty do to his law?" After a long time, 文帝 spoke with the 太后 about it, and then allowed the 廷尉's decision. At that time, 中尉 條侯 周亞夫 and 梁相 山都侯 王恬 were friendly with 張釋之 because he held a balanced opinion, and so became close friends. 張廷尉 was thus praised by the world.
After 文帝 died, 景帝 ascended the throne, and 張釋之 was afraid, claiming illness. He wanted to resign and leave, fearing that great punishment would come; he wanted to appear and apologize, but did not know how. Using 王生's plan, he finally appeared and apologized, and 景帝 did not blame him.
王生 was good at speaking 黃老, and was a 處士. He was once summoned to the 廷中, and the 三公 and 九卿 all gathered and stood. 王生, an old man, said, "My 韤 is untied," and turned to 張廷尉 and said, "Tie my 韤 for me!" 張釋之 knelt and tied it. Afterward, someone said to 王生, "Why did you alone humiliate 張廷尉, making him kneel and tie your 韤?" 王生 said, "I am old and lowly, I estimate that I will never benefit 張廷尉. 張廷尉 is now a famous minister of the world, so I merely humiliated the 廷尉, making him kneel and tie my 韤, wanting to honor him." The 諸公 heard of this, and praised 王生 and honored 張廷尉.
張廷尉 served 景帝 for more than a year, and was made 淮南王相, still regarding his past fault. After a long time, 張釋之 died. His son 張摯, courtesy name 長公, served as 大夫, and was dismissed. Because he could not gain favor with the times, he never served again in his life.
馮唐 was originally from 趙. His father moved to 代. When 漢 rose, he moved to 安陵. 馮唐 was famous for his filial piety, and was made 中郎署長, serving 文帝. 文帝 passed by in a 輦, and asked 馮唐, "Why do you, an old man, become a 郎? Where is your home?" 馮唐 answered fully and truthfully. 文帝 said, "When I was in 代, my 尚食監 高袪 often spoke to me of the worth of 趙將 李齊, who fought at 鉅鹿. Now whenever I eat, my mind is never not at 鉅鹿. Does your father know this?" 馮唐 answered, "He is not as good as 廉頗 and 李牧 as a general." The emperor said, "Why?" 馮唐 said, "My grandfather, when he was in 趙, was a 官 (卒) [率] 將, and was good at 李牧. My father, who was formerly 代相, was good at 趙將 李齊, and knew his character." The emperor, having heard of the character of 廉頗 and 李牧, was greatly pleased, and struck his thigh, saying, "Alas! I alone did not have the chance to be 廉頗 and 李牧 when I was his general, how could I worry about the 匈奴?" 馮唐 said, "My lord! Even if Your Majesty obtained 廉頗 and 李牧, he would not be able to use them." The emperor was angry, rose, and entered the 禁中. After a long time, he summoned 馮唐 and reproached him, saying, "How could you insult me before so many people, and have no private place?" 馮唐 apologized, saying, "A lowly person does not know 忌諱."
At that time, the 匈奴 had just made a great incursion into 朝那, killing the 北地都尉 卬. The emperor was concerned about the 胡 invasion, and finally again asked 馮唐, "How do you know that I cannot use 廉頗 and 李牧?" 馮唐 answered, "I have heard that in ancient times, when the 王者 sent a general, he would kneel and push the 轂, saying, 'Inside the 閫, I control it; outside the 閫, the 將軍 controls it.' Military merit, 爵賞 are all decided outside, and then reported back. This is not empty talk. My grandfather said that 李牧, as 趙將 stationed on the border, had the 軍市租 all used to feast the 士, and 賞賜 were decided outside, not disturbed from within. He entrusted responsibility and demanded success, so 李牧 was able to use his intelligence fully, sending out 選車 千三百乘, 彀騎 萬三千, 百金之士 十萬, and thus drove the 單于 north, defeated the 東胡, destroyed the 澹林, suppressed the 彊秦 in the west, and supported 韓 and 魏 in the south. At that time, 趙 was nearly 霸. Afterward, when 趙王 遷 ascended the throne, his mother was a 倡. When 遷 ascended the throne, he used 郭開's slander, and finally killed 李牧, appointing 顏聚 to replace him. Therefore, the army was defeated, the soldiers fled, and 趙 was captured and destroyed by 秦. Now I have secretly heard that 魏尚, as 雲中守, had the 軍市租 all used to feast the 士卒, [and] private funds, slaughtering a 牛 every five days, feasting 賓客 and 軍吏 and 舍人, and thus the 匈奴 avoided him from afar, not coming near the 雲中 border. Once the 虜 entered, 尚 led the 車騎 to attack them, killing many of them. The 士卒 are all sons of families, rising from the fields to serve in the army, how could they know the 尺籍 and 伍符? They fight all day, behead and capture 虜, and report 功 to the 莫府, but if one word does not correspond, the 文吏 ties them with the law. Their 賞 does not go out, but the officials strictly follow the law. I am foolish, and think that Your Majesty's law is too clear, the 賞 too light, the 罰 too heavy. Moreover, 雲中守 魏尚, because of his 上功 and 首虜, was six grades lower, and Your Majesty had him referred to the 吏, had his 爵削, and punished him with 作. From this, it can be said that even if Your Majesty obtained 廉頗 and 李牧, he would not be able to use them. I am truly foolish, and have offended 忌諱, 死罪死罪!" 文帝 was pleased. That day, he ordered 馮唐 to hold the 節 and pardon 魏尚, and again appointed him as 雲中守, and appointed 馮唐 as 車騎都尉, in charge of the 中尉 and the 郡國車士.
In the seventh year, 景帝 ascended the throne, and 馮唐 was made 楚相, and dismissed. 武帝 ascended the throne, sought 賢良, and recommended 馮唐. 馮唐 at that time was over ninety years old, and could no longer serve as an official, so he appointed his son 馮遂 as 郎. 馮遂, courtesy name 王孫, was also an extraordinary man, and was friendly with me.
太史公 said: 張季's words about 長者, to uphold the law without bending to personal opinion; 馮公's discussion of 將率, how delicious it is! How delicious it is! The saying goes, "Do not know a person, look at his friends." The two men's praises can be recorded in the 廊廟. The 書 says, "Not partial, not 黨, the 王道 is 蕩蕩; not 黨, not partial, the 王道 is 便便." 張季 and 馮公 are close to this. [end of text]


